#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082938 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "060e80f0-44bd-5378-9253-999548115dd9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Number of Permutations of Objects Chosen From a Group Fewer Than Ten"}] :question/id #uuid "258b1f90-1c19-5a19-b796-a7c1c894bf17" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-5673" :question/problem "In a horse race with $8$ horses, how many different ways can the gold, silver, and bronze medals be awarded?" :question/worked-solution "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n_{n}P_r = \\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\n$$\n\nThere are $8$ horses, so $n=8$. We want to select $3$ of those horses for gold, silver, and bronze, so we have $r=3$.\n\nTherefore, the number of different ways to award the medals is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n_{8}P_{3} &= (8!)/((8 - 3)!) \\\\\n&= \\frac{8!}{5!} \\\\\n&= \\frac{8 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 5!}{5!} \\\\\n&= 8 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 6 \\\\\n&= 336\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082939 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "256d3a08-0ade-51e9-887b-67250d5fae21" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Number of Permutations of Objects Chosen From a Group of at Least Ten"}] :question/id #uuid "5431e96c-87d1-517b-a565-9621a0b67913" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-5674" :question/problem "A company has $20$ employees. A total of $4$ employees are needed to fill the roles of president, vice president, treasurer, and secretary. How many different ways can this be achieved?" :question/worked-solution "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n_{n}P_r = \\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\n$$\n\nThere are $20$ employees, so $n=20$. We want to select $4$ of those employees to fill the roles of president, vice president, treasurer, and secretary, so we have $r=4$.\n\nTherefore, the number of different ways to fill the roles is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n_{20}P_{4} &= (20!)/((20 - 4)!) \\\\\n&= \\frac{20!}{16!} \\\\\n&= \\frac{20 \\cdot 19 \\cdot 18 \\cdot 17 \\cdot 16!}{16!} \\\\\n&= 20 \\cdot 19 \\cdot 18 \\cdot 17 \\\\\n&= 116280\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082940 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7c35604-c9f9-5077-bddc-fe9446ac45e6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Permutation Given Using Alternate Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "c72ffaba-7a68-5070-920d-fe241be5c797" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-5675" :question/problem "Evaluate $P(9,3)$." :question/worked-solution "The formula for ${}_nP_r$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_nP_r = \\dfrac {n!} {(n - r)!} \\,\n$$\n\n$P(9,3)$ means the same thing as $_{9}P_3$. Using the usual formula for ${}_nP_r$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(9, 3) &= (9!)/((9 - 3)!) \\\\\n&= \\frac{9!}{6!} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9 \\cdot 8 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 6!}{6!} \\\\\n&= 9 \\cdot 8 \\cdot 7 \\\\\n&= 504\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083024 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9c145aa-bcbf-54bd-ba88-93f10aeb00f0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Permutation"}] :question/id #uuid "a18e8e9a-da60-5a42-840a-60f83137c6e0" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-7457" :question/problem "Calculate the value of ${}_{11}P_2$." :question/worked-solution "The formula for ${}_nP_r$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_nP_r = \\dfrac {n!} {(n - r)!} \\,\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n={11}$ and $r=2$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel} \\begin{aligned} {}_{11}P_2 &= \\dfrac {11!} {(11 - 2)!} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {11!}{9!} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {11 \\cdot 10 \\cdot \\cancel{9!}} {\\cancel{9!}} \\\\[5pt] &= 11 \\cdot 10 \\\\[5pt] &= 110. \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "256d3a08-0ade-51e9-887b-67250d5fae21" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Number of Permutations of Objects Chosen F